# Bundled-package baggage: presentation assets, tests, and inert files that
# Pi's package-manager install UI would show but the VSIX never runs. These
# are narrow per-file globs — they do NOT filter node_modules/** broadly and
# never touch @earendil-works/** hoisted transitive deps.
node_modules/pi-web-access/pi-web-fetch-demo.mp4
node_modules/pi-web-access/banner.png
node_modules/pi-web-access/test/**
node_modules/pi-web-access/skills/**
node_modules/pi-mcp-adapter/banner.png
node_modules/pi-mcp-adapter/cli.js
node_modules/@mixmark-io/domino/test/**

# Cross-platform esbuild binaries, ~250 MB uncompressed. Pi 0.85 added
# `@earendil-works/chord`, which depends on `esbuild`; because Pi's shrinkwrap
# enumerates all 26 of esbuild's optional platform packages, npm installs every
# one of them instead of just the host's. A user can run exactly one, and none
# of them is reachable here: `chord` is referenced only from Pi's own
# `dist/bundle/` CLI chunks, while the extension host imports the package root
# (`dist/index.js`), whose graph never touches it. Keeping them more than
# doubled the VSIX (87 MB → 204 MB).
#
# The `esbuild` JS package itself is deliberately left in, so a code path that
# merely resolves it still finds a module. Narrow glob: this does not filter
# node_modules/** broadly and does not touch hoisted transitive deps.
node_modules/**/@esbuild/**
